{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Behold, a people like a lioness rises, etc.</b> When they rise from their sleep in the morning, they are mighty as a lioness and as a lion to snatch the commandments — to don the tallit, to recite Shema, and to lay tefillin." "<b>He does not lie down.</b> At night upon his bed until he has eaten and battered every foe that comes to devour him. How? He recites Shema upon his bed and commits his spirit into the hand of the Omnipresent; if a camp and army comes to harm them, the Holy One, blessed be He, guards them and wages their battles and fells them corpses (ibid.). Another interpretation — <b>Behold, a people like a lioness rises, etc.</b> — as the Targum renders." "<b>And the blood of the slain he drinks.</b> He prophesied that Moses would not die until he felled the kings of Midian as corpses, and that he [Moses] would be killed with them, as it is stated (Joshua 13): ״וְאֶת בִּלְעָם בֶּן בְּעוֹר הַקּוֹסֵם הָרְגוּ בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל בַּחֶרֶב אֶל חַלְלֵיהֶם״ (see Tanhuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:29.968847132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}